Expected elements: present

I found the focused control first: an outer box x81-197/y17-45, 2px stroke, square corners, interior fill byte-identical to the bar. And the expectation is wrong about it. This is not a UA ring — it is `styles.nim`'s one `:focus-visible` rule reaching the `[tabindex]` hydration added, painting `--bt-focus-ring`: **#3B82F6 = 3.68:1 on the #FFFFFF bar, #60A5FA = 6.77:1 on the #1B1B1B bar.** Both clear SC 1.4.11's 3:1 floor; dark is the stronger half. The design system does choose it, it theme-maps, and at the one moment it is drawn it is the loudest control chrome in the bar — 2.2x the `.dcbtn` outline in light (#C8C8C8, 1.67:1), 5.8x in dark (#282828, 1.17:1).

Colour signal of interactivity: exactly zero. Diffing this frame against the plain-build `debugger` capture gives **568 differing pixels of 2,073,600 — 0.027% — bbox x81-197/y17-45, the same count in both themes.** Hydration's entire visual contribution to a page carrying 39 `role="button"` controls is one focus ring on one of them.

The real colour defect is dark-only: #60A5FA is simultaneously the focus ring, the FETCHING phase ink (x1247-1303) and the `Synthetic demo data` provenance ink (x1752-1908), and sits 1.17:1 from the link indigo #818CF8.

Highest-priority fixes: move the dark ring off `colors.information.400`; give `.copybtn` a resting border in the `.dcbtn` vocabulary.

Rating: 6/10

